---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import HarnessesNav from '../../components/harnesses/HarnessesNav.astro';
import HarnessCard from '../../components/harnesses/HarnessCard.astro';
import {
  CATEGORY_COPY,
  harnessesByCategory,
  harnessPath,
  usedOnOurRig,
  type HarnessCategory,
} from '../../lib/harnesses';
import { harnesses, harnessesFile } from '../../lib/harnesses-data';

const all = harnesses();
const onRig = usedOnOurRig(all);
const categories = (Object.keys(CATEGORY_COPY) as HarnessCategory[]).map((id) => ({
  id,
  ...CATEGORY_COPY[id],
  rows: harnessesByCategory(all, id),
}));
---

<Base
  title="Harnesses & frontends"
  description="What to plug your local model into — agent harnesses, chat UIs, and ComfyUI on ROCm, talking to llama-server or Strata over an OpenAI-compatible API."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <HarnessesNav current="overview" />
    <h1 class="display mt-6 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Harnesses &amp; frontends: what to plug your local model into</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Path: <strong class="text-ink">your Radeon</strong> → a
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/models">tested model</a> →
      your agent (Hermes, Aider, Cline, OpenCode).
      A <strong class="text-ink">harness</strong> is the app or agent layer on top of an inference
      server. <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/backends">llama-server</a>,
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/stacks#fast-agent">Strata</a>,
      vLLM, and Ollama run the weights. The harness talks to them over an
      <strong class="text-ink">OpenAI-compatible API</strong>. It is not the GPU stack. If
      <code>/v1</code> is down, the harness is a very expensive timeout.
      Reliable tool calls and JSON from llama-server live on
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/guides/tool-calling">tool calling</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-faint">
      Cited from official repos and docs, checked {harnessesFile.as_of}. We do not invent features —
      unclear items stay “not documented.” Exact serve flags for our rig stay not recorded in
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/stacks">stacks</a>.
    </p>

    <pre class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-line bg-raised p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed" aria-label="Harness stack"><code>{`You  →  harness (tools, memory, channels, chat UI)
          →  HTTP  OpenAI-shaped /v1
            →  llama-server :8080  /  Strata :8083  /  vLLM :8000  /  Ollama :11434
              →  R9700 (Vulkan or HIP)`}</code></pre>

    <p class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/harnesses/connect">Copy-paste connect</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/harnesses/quiz">Pick a harness</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/harnesses/compare">Comparison table</a>
    </p>

    {onRig.length > 0 && (
      <section class="card mt-10 p-5" aria-labelledby="rig-heading">
        <p class="kicker">local-desktop</p>
        <h2 id="rig-heading" class="mt-1 text-xl tracking-tight">Used on our rig</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
          amdai’s daily agent on the two-R9700 box. Pointed at Strata
          <code>:{harnessesFile.strata_port}</code> and llama-server
          <code>:{harnessesFile.llama_server_port}</code>.
          Next to that house setup, Shannon (@iamMrDuncan) describes a multi-profile
          Hermes layout and Hermes desktop bot mode —
          <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/labs/shannon">cited, not measured by AMDai</a>.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          {onRig.map((row) => (
            <li>
              <a class="font-medium underline decoration-accent/40" href={harnessPath(row.id)}>{row.title}</a>
              <span class="ml-2 badge-tested">Used on our rig</span>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">{row.what_for}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    )}

    <Callout type="linux">
      On AMD, stand up <a href="/software">llama.cpp or vLLM</a> yourself. Do not let a harness
      download a CUDA llama.cpp “for convenience.” You own HIP/<code>gfx1201</code>; the harness
      only POSTs JSON. <code>curl</code> <code>/v1/models</code> before you debug the frontend.
    </Callout>

    <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="attach-heading">
      <h2 id="attach-heading" class="text-2xl tracking-tight">Attach after <code>/v1</code> is up</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">1.</strong> <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/tutorials/verify-rocm">Verify ROCm</a> — <code>rocminfo</code> shows <code>gfx1201</code>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">2.</strong> Serve official Qwen instruct — <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/tutorials/serve-qwen">Serve Qwen</a>. llama-server default is <code>127.0.0.1:{harnessesFile.llama_server_port}</code>. This site’s Strata convention is <code>:{harnessesFile.strata_port}</code>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">3.</strong> Prove the API on loopback. Snippets: <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/harnesses/connect">Connect</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">4.</strong> Watch a GPU meter during that completion. VRAM and compute must move.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">5.</strong> Then point the harness at that base URL. Model id must match <code>GET /v1/models</code> (placeholder on this site: <code>{harnessesFile.model_placeholder}</code>).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">6.</strong> Only after a chat turn works, enable tools that can touch the filesystem or the network.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/stack-lab">Radeon Stack Lab</a>
        <code>qwen-reliable</code> is the daily driver (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q5).
        <code>qwen-fast-agent</code> is Qwen 3.8 Flash on Strata. Cards:
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/stacks">recommended stacks</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="cat-heading">
      <h2 id="cat-heading" class="text-2xl tracking-tight">Categories</h2>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {categories.map((cat) => (
          <a class="card block p-5" href={cat.href}>
            <p class="kicker">{cat.rows.length} listed</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl tracking-tight">{cat.label}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{cat.lede}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    {categories.map((cat) => (
      <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby={`${cat.id}-heading`}>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-3">
          <h2 id={`${cat.id}-heading`} class="text-2xl tracking-tight">{cat.label}</h2>
          <a class="text-sm underline decoration-accent/40" href={cat.href}>All {cat.id}</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{cat.lede}</p>
        <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3">
          {cat.rows.map((row) => (
            <li>
              <HarnessCard row={row} />
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    ))}

    <section class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-line p-5" aria-labelledby="overnight-heading">
      <h2 id="overnight-heading" class="text-xl tracking-tight">Overnight research loop (this site’s YAML)</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
        Local Hermes is a practical overnight research agent for the living tracker. It does
        <strong class="text-ink"> not</strong> publish.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>Leave official instruct serving on <code>/v1</code> (the same URL you just curled).</li>
        <li>Attach Hermes to that endpoint — <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/harnesses/hermes">Hermes notes</a>.</li>
        <li>Point it at the weekday source list on <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/maintain">Weekday scrape</a>.</li>
        <li>Ask for a draft diff to the living YAML only. No invented benches. No download stats.</li>
        <li>In the morning: read the diff, run the smoke tests if a pin moved, <code>npm run build</code>, commit on <code>main</code>.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
